    "title": "Alabama defeats Nebraska 5-1 in NCAA Tournament with standout Braya Hodges on roster",
    "text": "On Saturday, May 30, the Alabama Crimson Tide, featuring former Houston Academy standout softball player Braya Hodges, earned a 5-1 victory over the Nebraska Cornhuskers in NCAA Tournament play.\nThe matchup was held at Devon Park, starting at 6 p.m.\nAlabama’s next tournament game is scheduled for Monday, June 1, also at 6 p.m. at Devon Park.\nBraya Hodges — Right handed pitcher — Sophomore — 5′8″ — Hometown: Dothan",
